ELEMENTARY TRANSCENDENTAL FUNCTIONS (p.1)
4.5.75  \frac{d}{dz}\,\mathrm{sech}\,z=-\mathrm{sech}\,z\tanh z
4.5.76  \frac{d}{dz}\,\mathrm{coth}\,z=-\mathrm{csch}^2\,z
Integration Formulas
4.5.77  \int\sinh\,z\,dz=\cosh\,z
4.5.78  \int\cosh\,z\,dz=\sinh\,z
4.5.79  \int\tanh\,z\,dz=\ln\cosh\,z
4.5.80  \int\mathrm{csch}\,z\,dz=\ln\tanh\frac{z}{2}
4.5.81  \int\mathrm{sech}\,z\,dz=\arctan\,(\sinh\,z)
4.5.82  \int\mathrm{coth}\,z\,dz=\ln\sinh\,z
4.5.83  \int z^n\sinh\,z\,dz=z^n\cosh\,z-n\int z^{n-1}\cosh\,z\,dz
4.5.84  \int z^n\cosh\,z\,dz=z^n\sinh\,z-n\int z^{n-1}\sinh\,z\,dz
4.5.85  \int\sinh^m\,z\cosh^n\,z\,dz=\frac{1}{m+n}\sinh^n+1\,z\cosh^n-1\,z
\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad+\frac{n-1}{m+n}\int\sinh^m\,z\cosh^n-2\,z\,dz
=\frac{1}{m+n}\sinh^m-1\,z\,\cosh^n+1\,z
\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad-\frac{m-1}{m+n}\sinh^m-2\,z\cosh^n+2\,(m+n\neq 0)
4.5.86  \int\frac{dz}{\sinh^m\,z\,\cosh^n}z=\frac{-1}{m-1}\frac{1}{\sinh^n-1\,z\,\cosh^n-1\,z}
\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad-\frac{m+n-2}{m-1}\int\frac{dz}{\sinh^n-2\,z\cosh^n-2\,z}\quad(m\neq 1)
(see chapters 5 and 7 for other integrals involving hyperbolic functions.)
4.6. Inverse Hyperbolic Functions Definitions
4.6.1  \arcsinh\,z=\int_{0}^{z}\frac{dt}{(1+t^2)^3}\qquad(z=x+iy)
4.6.2  \arccosh\,z=\int_{1}^{z}\frac{dt}{(t^2-1)^3}
4.6.3  \arctanh\,z=\int_{0}^{z}\frac{dt}{1-t^4}
The paths of integration must not cross the following cuts.
4.6.1 imaginary axis from -i\infty to -i and i to i\infty
4.6.2 real axis from -\infty to +1
4.6.3 real axis from -\infty to -1 and +1 to +\infty
Inverse hyperbolic functions are also written sinh^n+1\,z, arsinh z, Arsinh z, etc.
4.6.4  \arccosh\,z=\arcsinh\,1/z
4.6.5  \arccosh\,z=\arccosh\,1/z
4.6.6  \arccosh\,z=\arctanh\,1/z
